From: SP11 audio engineering closure
Subject: [PATCH 0026] SP11: add Windows-parity CPS feedback transport

Candidate-only patch generated 2026-08-11 against the reconstructed pre-CPS
effective SP11 v7.1.5 audio source. It intentionally keeps the physical
SoundWire master schedule on port 13, gives both WSA8845 DP6 slave ports
ChannelEnable 0x03, applies per-slave OffsetCtrl1 0/25, and opts DP6 into the
additional SIMPLE-port bank registers proven by the Windows qcaucd runtime
capture. It also adds the dedicated 24 kHz/S32 WSA TX1 CPS backend and gates
speaker protection on both VI and CPS readiness.

This patch is compile/DTB validated only. It has not been booted on SP11 Linux.

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wsa8840.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wsa8840.yaml
@@ -40,12 +40,24 @@
